    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "David also struck Hadadezer the son of Rehob, king of Zobah, as he went to recover his dominion at the River."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah, David struck twenty two thousand men of the Syrians."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "From Betah and from Berothai, cities of Hadadezer, King David took a great quantity of bronze."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Toi king of Hamath heard that David had struck all the army of Hadadezer,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "then Toi sent Joram his son to King David to greet him and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer and struck him; for Hadadezer had wars with Toi. Joram brought with him vessels of silver, vessels of gold, and vessels of bronze."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 8:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "of Syria, of Moab, of the children of Ammon, of the Philistines, of Amalek, and of the plunder of Hadadezer, son of Rehob, king of Zobah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 10:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hadadezer sent and brought out the Syrians who were beyond the River; and they came to Helam, with Shobach the captain of the army of Hadadezer at their head."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 10:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "When all the kings who were servants to Hadadezer saw that they were defeated before Israel, they made peace with Israel and served them. So the Syrians were afraid to help the children of Ammon any more."
      }
    ],
